diff --git a/abstract-sim-hs/README.md b/abstract-sim-hs/README.md
index 1d6f3fcf..56ce2738 100644
--- a/abstract-sim-hs/README.md
+++ b/abstract-sim-hs/README.md
@@ -3,13 +3,19 @@
 ## Canonical phase-2 recommendation
 
 The canonical simulator configuration for the phase-2 recommendation is
+[`config/variants/standard-window-confirm/block-window-10-cert-reset.json`](config/variants/standard-window-confirm/block-window-10-cert-reset.json).
+It combines the D16 controllers, the 0.75/0.5 targets, the 10-block
+processed-block standard window (announcements get no entry), the 5-sample
+urgent window, the half-RB announcement threshold, the K = 10 age escape
+with its count reset at certification, rb-only premium scope, absolute
+coefficient floor 1, and no cross-lane multiplier floor. The max-of-two
+fee-cap rule is the simulator's rb-only fee semantics rather than a
+configuration switch. The historical canonical configuration, with the
+20-entry announcement-diluted standard window and the announcement-time
+reset, is preserved at
 [`config/variants/trickle-aging/thr-k10.json`](config/variants/trickle-aging/thr-k10.json).
-It combines the D16 controllers, 20/5 signal windows, half-RB announcement
-threshold, K = 10 age escape, rb-only premium scope, absolute coefficient
-floor 1, and no cross-lane multiplier floor. The max-of-two fee-cap rule is
-the simulator's rb-only fee semantics rather than a configuration switch.
-Its embedded load is a default for direct runs; sweep load overrides do not
-change the recommended mechanism.
+Each file's embedded load is a default for direct runs; sweep load overrides
+do not change the recommended mechanism.
 
 Run the bounded post-correction launch-day integration check with:
 
diff --git a/abstract-sim-hs/config/sweeps/announcement-semantics-smoke.json b/abstract-sim-hs/config/sweeps/announcement-semantics-smoke.json
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..dd7915b5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/abstract-sim-hs/config/sweeps/announcement-semantics-smoke.json
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+{
+  "description": "Exploratory paired four-arm ablation of the simulator's announcement semantics against the CIP's specified semantics. Holds the S=.75/U=.50, D16, half-RB threshold, K10 mechanism fixed while varying two independent knobs: (1) block-window takes the standard controller's 20-entry window over processed-block summaries only, filtering out the zero-width EbAnnounced entries that the historical signal lets occupy window positions; (2) cert-reset restarts the EB age-escape count when a certified EB is applied, matching the specified 'Ranking Blocks since an EB certificate last entered the chain', instead of at every announcement (including announcements whose EB is later dropped without certifying). The fourth arm applies both. Ten paired seeds across the five headline loads plus the 0.1 tx/slot trickle (where the age escape binds) are intended as a directional smoke test, not confirmatory evidence.",
+  "seedStart": 440,
+  "seeds": 10,
+  "slots": 2000,
+  "summaryOnly": true,
+  "randomness": "independent-streams",
+  "out": "sweep-results/announcement-semantics-smoke/severe-congestion",
+  "variants": [
+    {
+      "name": "historical",
+      "config": "config/variants/standard-target-screen/s75-u50.json"
+    },
+    {
+      "name": "block-window",
+      "config": "config/variants/announcement-semantics/block-window.json"
+    },
+    {
+      "name": "cert-reset",
+      "config": "config/variants/announcement-semantics/cert-reset.json"
+    },
+    {
+      "name": "block-window-cert-reset",
+      "config": "config/variants/announcement-semantics/block-window-cert-reset.json"
+    }
+  ]
+}
